{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-baf533a6-df56-4541-9b98-147149dfebef","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f8402245511f952","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-55wpkne0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E003.md","content":"# odh-dashboard RBAC extension and feature flag manifests\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic extends the odh-dashboard's Kubernetes RBAC and dashboard configuration manifests so platform administrators can create, update, patch, and delete `FeatureStore` custom resources through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy, while non-admin (viewer) users retain read-only access enforced at the Kubernetes API level. It also introduces the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag that gates the Feature Store admin UI for progressive rollout.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Update `manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml` in the odh-dashboard repository: add `create`, `update`, `patch`, and `delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores` alongside the existing `get`, `list`, `watch`, using the feast-operator's `featurestore-editor-role` ClusterRole as the reference for the minimum required permission set.\n- Define the Feature Store admin UI feature flag default in OdhDashboardConfig so the admin pages can be progressively rolled out; clusters without the Feast component see no UI changes.\n- Verify the two authorization tiers end-to-end at the Kubernetes API level: admins operate on FeatureStore CRs with their own forwarded bearer token via kube-rbac-proxy; non-admin users are limited to the `featurestore-viewer-role` verb set (`get`, `list`, `watch` on `featurestores` and `featurestores/status`).\n- Keep the change manifest-only — no new backend routes, no new Go BFF module, no changes to FIPS-compliant build configuration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The odh-dashboard ClusterRole grants `create`, `update`, `patch`, and `delete` (in addition to the existing `get`, `list`, `watch`) on `feast.dev/featurestores`, and no verbs or resources beyond the minimum required set are added.\n- With the updated manifest applied, an admin test user can create and delete FeatureStore CRs through the dashboard's `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, verified via `kubectl auth can-i` for that user's bindings.\n- A non-admin (viewer) test user is denied create/update/patch/delete on `feast.dev/featurestores` at the Kubernetes API level (verified via `kubectl auth can-i`) — enforcement does not rely on UI-level hiding alone.\n- The Feature Store admin UI feature flag default is defined in OdhDashboardConfig; with the flag disabled, no Feature Store admin UI changes are visible in the dashboard.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-1 (P0 — admin create operations require the write verbs).\n- Enables HLR-4 (P0 — admin delete operations require the delete verb).\n- Enables HLR-6 (P1 — viewer read-only enforcement at the Kubernetes API level).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- RBAC enforcement remains at the Kubernetes API level via the user's forwarded token; the dashboard's `secureAdminRoute` middleware adds a UI-level check but is not the security boundary.\n- The admin CRUD acceptance criteria of the frontend implementation are jointly satisfiable only once both this manifest change and the frontend pages land — coordinate merge order even though the work streams are independent.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52767,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-866fdf02f8c7596b","agent_id":"a91c29e841bf56c68","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"aef3df60-bde5-4873-8106-0801e0e215b2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:11:46.656Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
