{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-19dbf5bf-de74-4041-881d-4d61937148ab","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1e33e7011ee5c7e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-55wpkne0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E004.md","content":"# Feature Store admin UI pages in odh-dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the Feature Store admin management surface in the RHOAI dashboard frontend: a management list page for FeatureStore instances, a guided create form wizard, a read-only instance detail/inspect view, a delete confirmation flow, and real-time deployment status tracking. The pages perform CRUD operations against the `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy, read Feast Registry metadata through the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy, and are gated behind the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Management list page: all FeatureStore CRs across namespaces accessible to the user, with columns for name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation timestamp; inspect and delete row actions; status updates in near real time using the dashboard's existing Kubernetes watch/list patterns without manual refresh.\n- Guided create wizard: PatternFly 6 form mapping to the TP field set recommended by the FeatureStore CRD validation work (namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling parameters); client-side validation against CRD schema constraints before submission; API-server rejection errors surfaced in the form. Reuse components of the engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) where the validation assessment confirms alignment.\n- Instance detail/inspect view: read-only rendering of the full FeatureStore CR spec and status — configured backends, registry type, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule, and deployment conditions — plus a link to the Feast UI Route when available.\n- Delete flow: confirmation dialog followed by a DELETE request through the `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; operator-side finalizer cleanup is relied upon for owned resources.\n- Viewer tier: create and delete controls hidden for non-admin users based on the dashboard's existing admin status check; non-admins see list and detail views only.\n- Feature flag gating via OdhDashboardConfig: with the flag disabled the pages are not rendered.\n- Disconnected/air-gapped support: all form options, validation rules, and UI assets bundled in the dashboard's static build — no external network fetches.\n- QE validation of the CRUD flows, admin-vs-viewer RBAC enforcement, and disconnected-cluster operation is part of this epic's completion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a logged-in platform administrator, opening the Feature Store management page and choosing to create an instance shows a guided form wizard with fields for namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling configuration; submitting it creates a valid `FeatureStore` CR via the Kubernetes API.\n- After submission, the management page shows the instance with a deploying status that transitions to ready as `.status.conditions` update, within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle and without manual refresh.\n- The list page shows all FeatureStore instances in the user's accessible namespaces with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` output for those namespaces.\n- The detail view renders all spec fields of the `FeatureStore` CR (backends, auth mode, scaling, TLS, materialization schedule) and current status conditions without truncation.\n- Deleting an instance from the confirmation dialog removes the CR; the instance disappears from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returns NotFound.\n- A non-admin (viewer) user sees the list and detail views but no create or delete controls.\n- The admin UI functions on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster: an instance can be deployed from the dashboard with no external network connectivity (validated by QE on an air-gapped environment).\n- Inline validation guidance is provided for CRD schema constraints (required fields, valid backend combinations per the validation report), and API-server rejection messages are surfaced in the form.\n- With the feature flag disabled, no Feature Store admin UI changes are visible.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Implements HLR-1 (P0 — create wizard), HLR-2 (P0 — management list page), HLR-3 (P0 — inspect/detail view), HLR-4 (P0 — delete flow), HLR-5 (P0 — deployment status tracking).\n- Implements HLR-6 (P1 — viewer read-only browsing), HLR-7 (P1 — disconnected/air-gapped operation), HLR-8 (P2 — inline validation guidance).\n- Depends on the finalized UX designs for the wizard, list, detail, and delete surfaces, and on the FeatureStore CRD validation report for the wizard field set and backend-combination restrictions.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- CRD schema changes between Feast versions could break wizard field mapping; mitigation: pin to feast.dev/v1 and derive validation rules from the CRD OpenAPI schema.\n- The dashboard pod already runs 9+ containers; this epic adds frontend pages only (no new BFF sidecar), with pod resource consumption monitored in QE environments.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":53633,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-866fdf02f8c7596b","agent_id":"a91c29e841bf56c68","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"06e6d824-1c53-40f3-a362-fe823c224153","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:12:02.888Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
