{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bff48641-f0c6-469f-8ffd-6557f41cf100","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b8f60fc6073d4a0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-55wpkne0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E005.md","content":"# Admin guide documentation for the Feature Store admin UI\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic documents the Feature Store admin UI workflow in the RHOAI admin guide: how a platform administrator deploys, monitors, inspects, and deletes Feature Store instances from the dashboard, including instructions for disconnected/air-gapped deployments. It is authored after the implementation is complete so the documentation describes what was actually built.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline:\n\n- New admin guide topic: deploying a Feature Store instance from the dashboard — when to use the guided create wizard, and field-by-field guidance for namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling configuration, including which backend combinations are production-ready.\n- Topic: monitoring and inspecting instances — the management list page, deployment status meanings (deploying, ready, degraded conditions), and the read-only detail view.\n- Topic: deleting a Feature Store instance — the confirmation flow and what the operator cleans up.\n- Topic: the viewer (non-admin) read-only experience.\n- Topic: disconnected/air-gapped deployment instructions — deploying and managing Feature Store instances from the dashboard on a cluster with no external network access.\n- Feature flag note for administrators: enabling/disabling the Feature Store admin UI via OdhDashboardConfig.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The admin guide documents the complete admin workflow: creating, monitoring, inspecting, and deleting Feature Store instances from the dashboard.\n- Disconnected/air-gapped deployment instructions are included and consistent with the shipped air-gapped behavior.\n- The viewer (non-admin) read-only experience is documented.\n- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented UI by engineering and the review findings are addressed.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Documents the workflows delivered by HLR-1 through HLR-7 (P0 create/list/inspect/delete/status; P1 viewer tier and air-gapped operation).\n- This is a documentation epic; it does not implement HLRs directly.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Content must not be finalized before the implementation is stable; this epic is deliberately sequenced last so the docs describe the shipped behavior.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":54857,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-866fdf02f8c7596b","agent_id":"a91c29e841bf56c68","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"dd101915-33ed-4951-a430-446209d30091","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:12:13.741Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
