{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ba83918f-1c2d-4881-86f9-6c2c00d8e4a1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bea671e1a9bd1e5d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-55wpkne0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-BRANCH-B-E006.md","content":"# feast-operator remediation for dashboard-submitted resources (conditional)\n\n## Description\n\nThis conditional epic exists only if the FeatureStore CRD and feast-operator validation investigation finds gaps that prevent the dashboard admin UI from working against the existing operator — for example, CRD/webhook validation that does not reject invalid UI-submitted resources with retrievable error messages, or reconciliation/cleanup behavior that differs for custom resources created through the Kubernetes API rather than kubectl. It remediates the identified gaps in the feast-operator (and, if required, the FeatureStore CRD) so dashboard-driven create, monitor, inspect, and delete flows work end to end.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Fix the specific operator/CRD gaps documented in the validation report — anticipated candidates: admission/webhook validation coverage for UI-submitted FeatureStore CRs, error message retrieval for API-server rejections, and finalizer-based cleanup of owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, RBAC, Routes) for dashboard-deleted instances.\n- Follow the upstream-first workflow for feast changes (feast-dev/feast upstream, opendatahub-io midstream, red-hat-data-services downstream) so the fix lands in the shipped RHOAI distribution.\n- Re-verify the affected flows with the dashboard once the fix is available.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every gap identified by the validation investigation is fixed, with each fix traceable to a documented finding.\n- Dashboard-submitted FeatureStore CRs that violate schema constraints are rejected by the API server/webhook with error messages the dashboard can retrieve and display.\n- The operator reconciles dashboard-created FeatureStore CRs identically to kubectl-created ones, and deletes clean up all owned resources.\n- The fixes are merged through the upstream/midstream/downstream flow and available in the RHOAI build consumed by the dashboard admin UI validation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Remediation support for HLR-1 (P0 — valid CR submission and validation feedback), HLR-4 (P0 — delete and cleanup), and HLR-5 (P0 — status conditions surfaced for tracking).\n- This epic is conditional: it implements HLR support only in the outcome where operator gaps are found.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- If the validation investigation confirms the operator and CRD already handle dashboard-created resources correctly, this epic is dropped and the main-plan dashboard implementation proceeds against the existing feast-operator unchanged.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55493,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-866fdf02f8c7596b","agent_id":"a91c29e841bf56c68","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"07386365-195a-47bc-9f54-3258fcea68d1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:12:24.017Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
