{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8917e0c195f4c5df","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8007\n11\t\n12\t**Strategy**: [TP] Feature Store Admin UI — Self-Service Instance Deployment and Management\n13\t**Triage**: Not below threshold (effort M / 3-5 sprints; spans frontend UI, RBAC/manifests, UXD design, docs, and cross-team validation — architecturally distinct work streams). Not docs-only (code changes in odh-dashboard).\n14\t\n15\t**Staff Engineer Input**: Section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides to apply.\n16\t\n17\t## Component Mapping Notes\n18\t\n19\tCanonical component names (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) assigned to strategy components:\n20\t\n21\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n22\t| --- | --- | --- |\n23\t| odh-dashboard (frontend / backend / manifests) | AI Core Dashboard | Closest canonical name; the strategy's three odh-dashboard rows (frontend, backend RBAC, kustomize manifests) all map here. |\n24\t| feast-operator | Feature Store | feast-operator is the Feast feature store operator; architecture context `feast.md` / `feast-module-operator.md` exist, so it is in-platform. |\n25\t| UXD design assets | UXD | Design work stream owned by the UXD team. |\n26\t| RHOAI admin guide | Documentation | Docs content work stream owned by the Documentation team. |\n27\t\n28\tBoth odh-dashboard and feast-operator have architecture context files — no new-component onboarding chain is required.\n29\t\n30\t## Epic List\n31\t\n32\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n33\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 | Validate FeatureStore CRD and feast-operator support for dashboard-driven lifecycle | Investigation | Fea