at the frontend epic builds. True gate: `rewrite` of wizard scope if the field set or validation constraints differ; `add_remediation` (branch B epic) if operator gaps are found. |\n65\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12 | The frontend builds against the UXD wireframes/interaction patterns (design artifact consumed by code). |\n66\t| E003 ∥ E001, E002, E004 | Rule 15 | RBAC/manifest change and frontend pages live in the same repo but different areas; the frontend does not build against the ClusterRole manifest (RBAC is enforced at the K8s API at runtime — an AC gate, not a build-against artifact). Coordinated via the wizard CRUD acceptance criteria. |\n67\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic. Direct edge needed because E003 is a root (E004 does not depend on it). |\n68\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | Docs describe what was built — always last. E002 is transitively blocking via E004. |\n69\t| E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14/15 | The UXD design starts from the prototype and the known CRD field list (strategy risk mitigation: \"engage UXD immediately; use the prototype as a starting design reference\"); field-set refinements from the investigation fold into design iteration. Kept parallel deliberately. |\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n72\t\n73\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic(s) |\n74\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n75\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Deploy new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard (namespace, registry type, online/offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling) | E004 (implemented; enabled by E001 field set, E002 designs, E003 RBAC) |\n76\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Management page listing all FeatureStore instances (name, namespace, status, creation time) | E004 |\n77\t| HLR-3 | P0 | Read-only inspect/detail view of instance configuration | E004 |\n78\t| HLR-4 | P0 | Delete instance from dashboard with confirmation dialog | E004 (RBAC verbs from E003; finalizer cleanup validated in E001) |\n79\t| HLR-5 | P0 | Deployment progress / readiness status visible in real time | E004 |\n80\t| HLR-6 | P1 | Viewers can browse but not create/delete | E004 (UI tier) + E003 (K8s-level enforcement) |\n81\t| HLR-7 | P1 | Functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments | E004 (bundled static assets; QE-validated AC) |\n82\t| HLR-8 | P2 | Inline form validation guidance for CRD schema constraints | E004 (constraints defined by E001) |\n83\t\n84\tAll 8 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. E005 documents the delivered workflows (HLR-1 through HLR-7).\n85\t\n86\t## Open Questions Disposition\n87\t\n88\t| Strategy open question / assumption | Disposition |\n89\t| --- | --- |\n90\t| Create form: all CRD fields vs curated TP subset | Investigation E001 (changes what the wizard builds — gates E004; PM + Feature Store Engineering input folded in) |\n91\t| Backend combinations to restrict in the form (e.g., SQLite dev-only) | Investigation E001 (deliverable: restriction list consumed as wizard validation rules) |\n92\t| Does prototype PR #7013 align with this strategy? | Investigation E001 (alignment assessment; reuse decision is an input to E004) |\n93\t| feast-operator \"no code changes expected\" + \"may need validation that CRD webhook validation is sufficient\" | Passive component validated by a different team → E001 (Investigation). Conditional branch B epic (E006) covers remediation if gaps are found. |\n94\t| Editing deployed instances for TP? | Resolved by strategy Out-of-Scope (\"Editing an existing FeatureStore instance\" is explicitly deferred) — no epic. Stale open question noted in Health Warnings. |\n95\t| Performance targets for TP? | Prerequisites table says Performance Team Support \"Not applicable\" — no epic, no AC. Noted in Health Warnings. |\n96\t| Platform admins have RBAC write permissions? | Resolved by this strategy's RBAC extension (E003 AC verifies with `kubectl auth can-i`). |\n97\t| CRD stability across Feast versions (pin feast.dev/v1) | Risk item — mitigation (pin v1, validate against