{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fa021dcba7cde0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n3\ttitle: Feature Store admin UI pages in odh-dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: -1\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\timplementation_type: null\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 4\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Feature Store admin UI pages in odh-dashboard\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the Feature Store admin management surface in the RHOAI dashboard frontend: a management list page for FeatureStore instances, a guided create form wizard, a read-only instance detail/inspect view, a delete confirmation flow, and real-time deployment status tracking. The pages perform CRUD operations against the `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy, read Feast Registry metadata through the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy, and are gated behind the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Management list page: all FeatureStore CRs across namespaces accessible to the user, with columns for name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation timestamp; inspect and delete row actions; status updates in near real time using the dashboard's existing Kubernetes watch/list patterns without manual refresh.\n40\t- Guided create wizard: PatternFly 6 form mapping to the TP field set recommended by the FeatureStore CRD validation work (namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling parameters); client-side validation against CRD schema constraints before submission; API-server rejection errors surfaced in the form. Reuse components of the engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) where the validation assessment confirms alignment.\n41\t- Instance detail/inspect view: read-only rendering of the full FeatureStore CR spec and status — configured backends, registry type, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule, and deployment conditions — plus a link to the Feast UI Route when available.\n42\t- Delete flow: confirmation dialog followed by a DELETE request through the `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; operator-side finalizer cleanup is relied upon for owned resources.\n43\t- Viewer tier: create and delete controls hidden for non-admin users based on the dashboard's existing admin status check; non-admins see list and detail views only.\n44\t- Feature flag gating via OdhDashboardConfig: with the flag disabled the pages are not rendered.\n45\t- Disconnected/air-gapped support: all form options, validation rules, and UI assets bundled in the dashboard's static build — no external network fetches.\n46\t- QE validation of the CRUD flows, admin-vs-viewer RBAC enforcement, and disconnected-cluster operation is part of this epic's completion.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given a logged-in platform administrator, opening the Feature Store management page and choosing to create an instance shows a guided form wizard with fields for namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling configuration; submitting it creates a valid `FeatureStore` CR via the Kubernetes API.\n51\t- After submission, the management page shows the instance with a deploying status that transitions to ready as `.status.conditions` update, within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle and without manual refresh.\n52\t- The list page shows all FeatureStore instances in the user's accessible namespaces with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` output for those namespaces.\n53\t- The detail view renders all spec fields of the `FeatureStore` CR (backends, auth mode, scaling, TLS, materialization schedule) and current status conditions without truncation.\n54\t- Deleting an instance from the confirmation dialog removes the CR; the instance disappears from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returns NotFound.\n55\t- A non-admin (viewer) user sees the list and detail views but no create or delete controls.\n56\t- The admin UI functions on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster: an instance can be deployed from the dashboard with no external network connectivity (validated by QE on an air-gapped environment).\n57\t- Inline validation guidance is provided for CRD schema constraints (required fields, valid backend combinations per the validation report), and API-server rejection messages are surfaced in the form.\n58\t- With the feature flag disabled, no Feature Store admin UI changes are visible.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- Implements HLR-1 (P0 — create wizard), HLR-2 (P0 — management list page), HLR-3 (P0 — inspect/detail view), HLR-4 (P0 — delete flow), HLR-5 (P0 — deployment status tracking).\n63\t- Implements HLR-6 (P1 — viewer read-only browsing), HLR-7 (P1 — disconnected/air-gapped operation), HLR-8 (P2 — inline validation guidance).\n64\t- Depends on the finalized UX designs for the wizard, list, detail, and delete surfaces, and on the FeatureStore CRD validation report for the wizard field set and backend-combination restrictions.\n65\t\n66\t## Risks / Notes\n67\t\n68\t- CRD schema changes between Feast versions could break wizard field mapping; mitigation: pin to feast.dev/v1 and derive validation rules from the CRD OpenAPI schema.\n69\t- The dashboard pod already runs 9+ containers; this epic adds frontend pages only (no new BFF sidecar), with pod resource consumption monitored in QE environments.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5be98dd36caa8eb","agent_id":"af290d82379028f6a","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"29709b04-c9ed-4f4c-8c2f-29ef1712c14d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:15:12.632Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fa021dcba7cde0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
