tent with it. P2 HLR-8 (inline validation) is covered by E004 with the constraint source (E001's validation report) identified, not deferred. Priority inheritance holds: E001 and E002 (both P0) gate the P0 frontend epic E004; E005 is a docs-authoring epic and is exempt (its P1 derives from the strategy's Major Jira priority — correct per the docs-authoring exception). No lower-priority epic blocks P0 work. Priority collapse considered and not flagged: the P1 HLRs (viewer read-only tier, air-gapped operation) and P2 HLR-8 are thin increments on the same admin UI surface built by E004, not independently deferrable features — splitting them out would create the same-surface split problem flagged under Criterion 3.\n39\t\n40\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n41\tDiagram edges (E001→E004, E002→E004, E003→E005, E004→E005) exactly match frontmatter `dependencies` (E004: [E001, E002]; E005: [E003, E004]; all others empty), and arrow direction follows the dependency→dependent convention. No cycles, no invalid edges. Each edge is justified: E001→E004 is a true investigation gate; E002→E004 is a design-artifact-consumed-by-code edge (Rule 12); E003→E005 and E004→E005 satisfy Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all implementations, with the direct E003 edge correctly added because E004 does not depend on E003). The deliberate E003∥E004 parallelism is correct: the frontend does not build against the ClusterRole manifest — RBAC applies at runtime via the K8s API, making it an AC gate rather than a build artifact, and both epics state the joint merge-order coordination. Critical path length 3 fits the M-standard heuristic (3-4). Branch epic BRANCH-B-E006 correctly sets both `branch: B` and `gated_by: E001` (present in its direct dependencies) with a populated gate_failure_impact, and no main-plan epic depends on the branch node — work hinging on the outcome depends on E001 itself. No data/artifact dependencies found in epic content that are missing from the DAG.\n42\t\n43\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n44\tEach epic is a clean component/team tuple: E001 (Feature Store / Feature Store Engineering), E002 (UXD / UXD Team), E003 and E004 (AI Core Dashboard / Dashboard/Frontend Engineering), E005 (Documentation / Documentation Team), branch E006 (Feature Store / Feature Store Engineering). No cross-team bundling. Work-product types are properly separated: design assets (E002), code+manifests (E003/E004), and content authoring (E005) are distinct epics. No scope duplication between siblings — E002 produces designs, E004 implements them; E003's RBAC verification and E004's UI-level viewer tier address different layers (K8s API vs. frontend) per the strategy's two-tier authorization model. One minor observation: E004 bundles the list page, wizard, detail view, delete flow, viewer tier, and QE validation — at the upper end of the ~2-week guideline, though defensible as one coherent surface for one team with a validated prototype (PR #7013) to reuse.\n45\t\n46\t### 4. Type Correctness (1/2)\n47\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (TP field set, backend restrictions, operator/webhook gap assessment) changes what E004 builds and whether branch E006 exists, and it has downstream dependents. E002/E003/E004/E005/E006 are Implementation epics producing concrete artifacts (design spec, manifests, UI pages, docs, operator fixes). Gating graph is otherwise correct: E004 and BRANCH-B-E006 both list E001 in `dependencies` and both set `gated_by: E001`; the branch epic's gate_failure_impact has both `action` and `fallback_approach` populated. Defect: **E004 sets `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001` but leaves `gate_failure_impact: null`** — the failure impact (rewrite of wizard scope; activation of branch B remediation) is documented only in the decomposition summary's DAG justification, not in the epic frontmatter where pipeline consumers read it. This is the rubric's canonical \"gated_by set without gate_failure_impact\" metadata issue; the gate itself is real (failure changes E004's scope), so it is not a mere scheduling dependency.\n48\t\n49\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n50\tType-appropriate signal fields are used throughout: E001 carries `investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric) with `ai_signals: null`; all Implementation epics carry `ai_signals` with `investigation_signals: null`. Signal values are consistent with the strategy content and the rationales match the frontmatter values: E001's `human_judgment_required: -1` correctly isolates the PM curated-subset decision while keeping `source_accessibility: 1` (the technical questions are answerable from readable source); E002's `human_process_gates: -1` and `open_questions: -1` reflect the UXD sign-off gate and pending field-set decision; E004's `open_questions: -1` matches its dependence on the investigation outcome while E003's `open_questions: 1` matches its fully-resolved manifest scope; branch E006's `external_dependency: -1` correctly captures the upstream-first Feast workflow. No signal contradicts the rubric conditions; no ai-signals file is missing.\n51\t\n52\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n53\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy's proposed acceptance criteria. Rule-mandated ACs are present where applicable: E005 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review AC; E003 verifies RBAC with `kubectl auth can-i` for both admin and viewer tiers (testable, matching the strategy's viewer-enforcement risk mitigation); E004 includes the feature-flag AC and the air-gapped QE validation AC. No replacement/konflux chain applies. No AC states an external schedule constraint — the UXD capacity risk is correctly placed in Health Warnings and E002's Risks/Notes rather than misfiled as an AC. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID; upstream work is referred to descriptively (\"the FeatureStore CRD validation work\", \"the UXD designs\").\n54\t\n55\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n56\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: create wizard, list page, detail view, delete flow, real-time status, viewer tier, air-gapped support, and inline validation all land in E004 with enabling work in E001/E002/E003; the RBAC extension and feature flag are in E003; docs (including disconnected deployment instructions, required by the strategy's Documentation Support prerequisite and Impacted Teams) are in E005. Every strategy open question and \"needs validation\" assumption has an explicit disposition — the technical unknowns route to E001, the stale editing question and undefined performance targets are explicitly noted in Health Warnings rather than silently dropped, and the RBAC write-permission assumption is resolved by E003's AC. Strategy risks are carried into epic risks/ACs (UXD delay, CRD version stability, air-gapped validation completeness, pod resource growth, viewer RBAC bypass). The conditional branch covers the bounded outcome of its investigation (operator gaps found → remediation epic; not found → dropped, with the fallback stated). Out-of-scope items (editing, permissions UI, multi-tenant) are correctly excluded. E001's seven scope items are each consumed downstream (field set and backend restrictions → E004 wizard/validation; RBAC verb confirmation → E003; prototype alignment → E004 reuse decision; reconciliation/webhook gaps → branch E006).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af10e0a7384597dc","agent_id":"a669e8a438b1bb436","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"198d3cb3-591c-4a99-90dd-84841e64d034","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:18:14.333Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88abbba3dc8808c6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
