{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bccd5c5ad9c59b8e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8007\n11\t\n12\t**Strategy**: [TP] Feature Store Admin UI — Self-Service Instance Deployment and Management\n13\t**Triage**: Not below threshold (effort M / 3-5 sprints; spans frontend UI, RBAC/manifests, UXD design, docs, and cross-team validation — architecturally distinct work streams). Not docs-only (code changes in odh-dashboard).\n14\t\n15\t**Staff Engineer Input**: Section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides to apply.\n16\t\n17\t## Component Mapping Notes\n18\t\n19\tCanonical component names (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) assigned to strategy components:\n20\t\n21\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n22\t| --- | --- | --- |\n23\t| odh-dashboard (frontend / backend / manifests) | AI Core Dashboard | Closest canonical name; the strategy's three odh-dashboard rows (frontend, backend RBAC, kustomize manifests) all map here. |\n24\t| feast-operator | Feature Store | feast-operator is the Feast feature store operator; architecture context `feast.md` / `feast-module-operator.md` exist, so it is in-platform. |\n25\t| UXD design assets | UXD | Design work stream owned by the UXD team. |\n26\t| RHOAI admin guide | Documentation | Docs content work stream owned by the Documentation team. |\n27\t\n28\tBoth odh-dashboard and feast-operator have architecture context files — no new-component onboarding chain is required.\n29\t\n30\t## Epic List\n31\t\n32\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n33\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 | Validate FeatureStore CRD and feast-operator support for dashboard-driven lifecycle | Investigation | Feature Store Engineering | Feature Store | P0 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 | UXD design for Feature Store admin UI (wizard, list, detail, delete) | Implementation | UXD Team | UXD | P0 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 | odh-dashboard RBAC extension and feature flag manifests | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | AI Core Dashboard | P0 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 | Feature Store admin UI pages in odh-dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | AI Core Dashboard | P0 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 | Admin guide documentation for the Feature Store admin UI | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation Team | Documentation | P1 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-BRANCH-B-E006 | feast-operator remediation for dashboard-submitted resources (conditional) | Implementation (branch B) | Feature Store Engineering | Feature Store | P0 |\n40\t\n41\tMain-plan epics: 5. Branch epic: 1 (conditional, not a standalone Jira issue).\n42\t\n43\t## Dependency DAG\n44\t\n45\t```mermaid\n46\tgraph TD\n47\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: FeatureStore CRD/operator validation\"]\n48\t    E002[\"E002 UXD design for admin UI\"]\n49\t    E003[\"E003 RBAC extension + feature flag manifests\"]\n50\t    E004[\"E004 Feature Store admin UI pages\"]\n51\t    E005[\"E005 Admin guide documentation\"]\n52\t    E001 --> E004\n53\t    E002 --> E004\n54\t    E003 --> E005\n55\t    E004 --> E005\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\tBranch epic (not a main-plan node): `RHAISTRAT-8007-BRANCH-B-E006` (feast-operator remediation) is gated by E001 and exists only if the investigation finds operator/CRD gaps. No main-plan epic depends on it; epics depending on the investigation outcome depend on E001 itself.\n59\t\n60\t## DAG Justification\n61\t\n62\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n63\t| --- | --- | --- |\n64\t| E001 → E004 | Step 3 / Rule 3, 12 | The investigation determines the create wizard's TP field set, backend-combination restrictions, and whether operator/webhook validation handles UI-submitted CRs — i.e., what the frontend epic builds. True gate: `rewrite` of wizard scope if the field set or validation constraints differ; `add_remediation` (branch B epic) if operator gaps are found. |\n65\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12 | The frontend builds against the UXD wireframes/interaction patterns (design artifact consumed by code). |\n66\t| E003 ∥ E001, E002, E004 | Rule 15 | RBAC/manifest change and frontend pages live in the same repo but different areas; the frontend does not build against the ClusterRole manifest (RBAC is enforced at the K8s API at runtime — an AC gate, not a build-against artifact). Coordinated via the wizard CRUD acceptance criteria. |\n67\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic. Direct edge needed because E003 is a root (E004 does not depend on it). |\n68\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | Docs describe what was built — always last. E002 is transitively blocking via E004. |\n69\t| E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14/15 | The UXD design starts from the prototype and the known CRD field list (strategy risk mitigation: \"engage UXD immediately; use the prototype as a starting design reference\"); field-set refinements from the investigation fold into design iteration. Kept parallel deliberately. |\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n72\t\n73\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic(s) |\n74\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n75\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Deploy new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard (namespace, registry type, online/offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling) | E004 (implemented; enabled by E001 field set, E002 designs, E003 RBAC) |\n76\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Management page listing all FeatureStore instances (name, namespace, status, creation time) | E004 |\n77\t| HLR-3 | P0 | Read-only inspect/detail view of instance configuration | E004 |\n78\t| HLR-4 | P0 | Delete instance from dashboard with confirmation dialog | E004 (RBAC verbs from E003; finalizer cleanup validated in E001) |\n79\t| HLR-5 | P0 | Deployment progress / rea