CRD OpenAPI schema) captured as AC/scope in E001 and E004. |\n98\t| UXD timeline | Schedule risk, not a technical unknown — Health Warning; design work is E002 on the critical path. |\n99\t\n100\t## Health Warnings\n101\t\n102\t- **Schedule risk — UXD capacity**: the `needs-uxd` label is queued but no design sprint is scheduled; E002 is on the critical path for the P0 frontend epic. Mitigation per strategy: start from prototype PR #7013 as design reference.\n103\t- **Stale open question**: the strategy asks whether editing deployed instances should be in TP scope while Out-of-Scope explicitly defers editing. Decomposition follows Out-of-Scope (create/inspect/delete only). If PM later pulls editing into scope, a new epic is needed.\n104\t- **Performance targets undefined**: open question acknowledges no perf targets exist; prerequisites mark performance support \"Not applicable\" for TP. List-page behavior with 100+ instances is untested — flagged for QE attention rather than an epic.\n105\t- **RBAC/frontend coordination**: E003 and E004 run in parallel by design (no DAG edge); the admin CRUD acceptance criteria on the frontend epic are only jointly satisfiable once both land — coordinate merge order in sprint planning.\n106\t- **QE involvement**: functional CRUD testing, RBAC enforcement, and disconnected-cluster validation are captured as acceptance criteria on E004 rather than a separate QE epic (QE is a verification role here, not an affected-component owner).\n107\t\n108\t## Tiered Delivery\n109\t\n110\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing gates user-facing value. All listed dependencies exist in-platform (CRD, operator, dashboard proxies, PatternFly 6, prototype PR). The only conditional work is investigation-gated (branch B), not external-vendor-gated.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af90472888fa9bb6","agent_id":"a10e9db46b4e557b2","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"8350accf-5d53-4fdb-9fe7-ce2de2