{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-912b4d921851e4fb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n3\ttitle: UXD design for Feature Store admin UI (wizard, list, detail, delete)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: UXD\n6\tteam: UXD Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: -1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# UXD design for Feature Store admin UI (wizard, list, detail, delete)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the UX design assets for the Feature Store admin management surface in the RHOAI dashboard: wireframes and interaction patterns for the guided create wizard, the management list page, the read-only instance detail view, and the delete confirmation dialog. The designs are the artifact the dashboard frontend implementation builds against, and use the validated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) as the starting design reference.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Wireframes and interaction patterns for the guided create form wizard: namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters, with inline validation guidance patterns for CRD schema constraints.\n38\t- Wireframes and interaction patterns for the management list page: instance rows showing name, namespace, deployment status, and creation timestamp; inspect and delete actions; status presentation for the deploying-to-ready progression.\n39\t- Wireframes for the read-only instance detail/inspect view (backends, authorization mode, scaling, TLS status, materialization schedule, deployment conditions).\n40\t- Interaction design for the delete confirmation dialog.\n41\t- Viewer (non-admin) variant of the list and detail views: read-only presentation with no create or delete controls.\n42\t- Disconnected/air-gapped constraint: designs must reference only assets bundled in the dashboard's static build — no external resource fetches.\n43\t- Design review iterations with product management and dashboard engineering, culminating in a signed-off design spec.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Finalized, reviewed wireframes exist for the create wizard covering all required fields: namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling configuration.\n48\t- Finalized, reviewed wireframes exist for the management list page, read-only detail view, and delete confirmation dialog.\n49\t- The viewer (non-admin) read-only variant is specified, with no create or delete controls presented.\n50\t- Inline validation and error-presentation patterns for form constraints are specified.\n51\t- The design spec passes formal UXD review and is signed off for implementation.\n52\t- No design element depends on fetching external network resources at runtime.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- Enables HLR-1 through HLR-5 (P0 — the UI surfaces the frontend implements).\n57\t- Enables HLR-6 (P1 — viewer read-only variant) and HLR-8 (P2 — inline validation guidance patterns).\n58\t\n59\t## Risks / Notes\n60\t\n61\t- The `needs-uxd` label is queued with no design sprint scheduled yet; the strategy directs engaging UXD immediately and using the prototype as the starting reference to avoid blocking.\n62\t- Wizard field-level wireframes may need one refinement iteration once the recommended TP field set (from the FeatureStore CRD validation work) is finalized; the two efforts run in parallel by design.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af90472888fa9bb6","agent_id":"a10e9db46b4e557b2","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"39432797-5c2f-442a-b05b-56da23304326","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:19:32.853Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-912b4d921851e4fb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
