{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d29d6b5e9eb7959","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n3\ttitle: odh-dashboard RBAC extension and feature flag manifests\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# odh-dashboard RBAC extension and feature flag manifests\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic extends the odh-dashboard's Kubernetes RBAC and dashboard configuration manifests so platform administrators can create, update, patch, and delete `FeatureStore` custom resources through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy, while non-admin (viewer) users retain read-only access enforced at the Kubernetes API level. It also introduces the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag that gates the Feature Store admin UI for progressive rollout.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Update `manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml` in the odh-dashboard repository: add `create`, `update`, `patch`, and `delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores` alongside the existing `get`, `list`, `watch`, using the feast-operator's `featurestore-editor-role` ClusterRole as the reference for the minimum required permission set.\n38\t- Define the Feature Store admin UI feature flag default in OdhDashboardConfig so the admin pages can be progressively rolled out; clusters without the Feast component see no UI changes.\n39\t- Verify the two authorization tiers end-to-end at the Kubernetes API level: admins operate on FeatureStore CRs with their own forwarded bearer token via kube-rbac-proxy; non-admin users are limited to the `featurestore-viewer-role` verb set (`get`, `list`, `watch` on `featurestores` and `featurestores/status`).\n40\t- Keep the change manifest-only — no new backend routes, no new Go BFF module, no changes to FIPS-compliant build configuration.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- The odh-dashboard ClusterRole grants `create`, `update`, `patch`, and `delete` (in addition to the existing `get`, `list`, `watch`) on `feast.dev/featurestores`, and no verbs or resources beyond the minimum required set are added.\n45\t- With the updated manifest applied, an admin test user can create and delete FeatureStore CRs through the dashboard's `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, verified via `kubectl auth can-i` for that user's bindings.\n46\t- A non-admin (viewer) test user is denied create/update/patch/delete on `feast.dev/featurestores` at the Kubernetes API level (verified via `kubectl auth can-i`) — enforcement does not rely on UI-level hiding alone.\n47\t- The Feature Store admin UI feature flag default is defined in OdhDashboardConfig; with the flag disabled, no Feature Store admin UI changes are visible in the dashboard.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- Enables HLR-1 (P0 — admin create operations require the write verbs).\n52\t- Enables HLR-4 (P0 — admin delete operations require the delete verb).\n53\t- Enables HLR-6 (P1 — viewer read-only enforcement at the Kubernetes API level).\n54\t\n55\t## Risks / Notes\n56\t\n57\t- RBAC enforcement remains at the Kubernetes API level via the user's forwarded token; the dashboard's `secureAdminRoute` middleware adds a UI-level check but is not the security boundary.\n58\t- The admin CRUD acceptance criteria of the frontend implementation are jointly satisfiable only once both this manifest change and the frontend pages land — coordinate merge order even though the work streams are independent.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af90472888fa9bb6","agent_id":"a10e9db46b4e557b2","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"f19f118e-0533-483e-841e-6f389325c917","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:19:36.270Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d29d6b5e9eb7959","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
