{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-837a9441641147cd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n3\ttitle: Admin guide documentation for the Feature Store admin UI\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Documentation Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 0\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 0\n22\t  architecture_claims: 0\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 2\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Admin guide documentation for the Feature Store admin UI\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic documents the Feature Store admin UI workflow in the RHOAI admin guide: how a platform administrator deploys, monitors, inspects, and deletes Feature Store instances from the dashboard, including instructions for disconnected/air-gapped deployments. It is authored after the implementation is complete so the documentation describes what was actually built.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\tContent outline:\n40\t\n41\t- New admin guide topic: deploying a Feature Store instance from the dashboard — when to use the guided create wizard, and field-by-field guidance for namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling configuration, including which backend combinations are production-ready.\n42\t- Topic: monitoring and inspecting instances — the management list page, deployment status meanings (deploying, ready, degraded conditions), and the read-only detail view.\n43\t- Topic: deleting a Feature Store instance — the confirmation flow and what the operator cleans up.\n44\t- Topic: the viewer (non-admin) read-only experience.\n45\t- Topic: disconnected/air-gapped deployment instructions — deploying and managing Feature Store instances from the dashboard on a cluster with no external network access.\n46\t- Feature flag note for administrators: enabling/disabling the Feature Store admin UI via OdhDashboardConfig.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The admin guide documents the complete admin workflow: creating, monitoring, inspecting, and deleting Feature Store instances from the dashboard.\n51\t- Disconnected/air-gapped deployment instructions are included and consistent with the shipped air-gapped behavior.\n52\t- The viewer (non-admin) read-only experience is documented.\n53\t- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented UI by engineering and the review findings are addressed.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Documents the workflows delivered by HLR-1 through HLR-7 (P0 create/list/inspect/delete/status; P1 viewer tier and air-gapped operation).\n58\t- This is a documentation epic; it does not implement HLRs directly.\n59\t\n60\t## Risks / Notes\n61\t\n62\t- Content must not be finalized before the implementation is stable; this epic is deliberately sequenced last so the docs describe the shipped behavior.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af90472888fa9bb6","agent_id":"a10e9db46b4e557b2","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"ec2292ca-347b-49f2-a06c-6fa06caac691","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:19:40.896Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-837a9441641147cd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
