{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae375ed8c6dfa590","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: feast-operator remediation for dashboard-submitted resources (conditional)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: Feature Store Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: add_remediation\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the validation confirms the feast-operator and FeatureStore\n16\t    CRD already handle dashboard-created resources correctly, this remediation epic\n17\t    is dropped and the dashboard implementation proceeds against the existing operator\n18\t    unchanged.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# feast-operator remediation for dashboard-submitted resources (conditional)\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis conditional epic exists only if the FeatureStore CRD and feast-operator validation investigation finds gaps that prevent the dashboard admin UI from working against the existing operator — for example, CRD/webhook validation that does not reject invalid UI-submitted resources with retrievable error messages, or reconciliation/cleanup behavior that differs for custom resources created through the Kubernetes API rather than kubectl. It remediates the identified gaps in the feast-operator (and, if required, the FeatureStore CRD) so dashboard-driven create, monitor, inspect, and delete flows work end to end.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Fix the specific operator/CRD gaps documented in the validation report — anticipated candidates: admission/webhook validation coverage for UI-submitted FeatureStore CRs, error message retrieval for API-server rejections, and finalizer-based cleanup of owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, RBAC, Routes) for dashboard-deleted instances.\n44\t- Follow the upstream-first workflow for feast changes (feast-dev/feast upstream, opendatahub-io midstream, red-hat-data-services downstream) so the fix lands in the shipped RHOAI distribution.\n45\t- Re-verify the affected flows with the dashboard once the fix is available.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Every gap identified by the validation investigation is fixed, with each fix traceable to a documented finding.\n50\t- Dashboard-submitted FeatureStore CRs that violate schema constraints are rejected by the API server/webhook with error messages the dashboard can retrieve and display.\n51\t- The operator reconciles dashboard-created FeatureStore CRs identically to kubectl-created ones, and deletes clean up all owned resources.\n52\t- The fixes are merged through the upstream/midstream/downstream flow and available in the RHOAI build consumed by the dashboard admin UI validation.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- Remediation support for HLR-1 (P0 — valid CR submission and validation feedback), HLR-4 (P0 — delete and cleanup), and HLR-5 (P0 — status conditions surfaced for tracking).\n57\t- This epic is conditional: it implements HLR support only in the outcome where operator gaps are found.\n58\t\n59\t## Risks / Notes\n60\t\n61\t- If the validation investigation confirms the operator and CRD already handle dashboard-created resources correctly, this epic is dropped and the main-plan dashboard implementation proceeds against the existing feast-operator unchanged.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af90472888fa9bb6