dation polish on the same wizard) are increments on the P0 surfaces, not independently plannable features, so bundling is correct.\n\n### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n\nDiagram edges (E001→E004, E002→E004, E003→E005, E004→E005) match epic frontmatter `dependencies` exactly (E004: [E001, E002]; E005: [E003, E004]; E001/E002/E003 roots), with arrows drawn dependency→dependent per convention. No cycles; all referenced epics exist. Critical path length 3 is within the M-standard heuristic (3–4). Each edge is justified: E001→E004 is a genuine investigation gate (Rule 3, gate action `rewrite` recorded); E002→E004 is a build-against design artifact (Rule 12); E003→E005 and E004→E005 satisfy Rule 11 (E002 transitively blocking via E004). Parallelism is correctly preserved: E001∥E002 (justified by the strategy's own risk mitigation — start UXD from the prototype), and E003∥E004 (Rule 15, same repo different areas; RBAC is runtime enforcement, an AC gate not a build-against artifact — the coupling is correctly captured as joint acceptance criteria plus a health warning rather than a serializing edge). No `konflux-onboarding`, `license-validation`, or `repo-onboarding` epics exist, so rules 7/8/10 are not applicable. Branch file RHAISTRAT-8007-BRANCH-B-E006 sets both `branch: B` (matching filename) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001` (present in its direct `dependencies`), and no main-plan epic lists the branch epic in `dependencies`. Cross-checked epic content for unlisted data/artifact dependencies — none found beyond the documented edges.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n\nEach epic has a clean component/team tuple: E001 and BRANCH-B-E006 (Feature Store / Feature Store Engineering), E002 (UXD / UXD Team), E003+E004 (AI Core Dashboard / Dashboard/Frontend Engineering), E005 (Documentation / Documentation Team) — all canonical names present in `.context/rhai-components.txt`. No epic spans multiple components or teams. No scope duplication across siblings: E002 designs the surfaces