e CRD OpenAPI schema, operator source, and prototype PR — the one PM decision is peripheral and separable), local_runnability 0 (controller verification genuinely needs a cluster/API server), cluster_hardware_dependence -1 (only peripheral questions need a live test cluster), human_judgment_required -1 (peripheral PM curated-subset decision). Implementation signal values are consistent with strategy content and the rationales: E002's human_process_gates -1 (formal UXD sign-off) and open_questions -1 (field-set question affects wireframes); E003's open_questions +1 (verbs, resource, and mechanism all fixed by the strategy); E004's open_questions -1 and human_process_gates -1 (investigation-dependent field set, UXD sign-off); E006's change_specificity 0 / external_dependency -1 (scope unknown until the investigation reports; upstream-first feast workflow). Rationale files exist for all six epics and match the frontmatter values. Computed totals/classifications not checked per instructions.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable, deliverable-scoped ACs. Rule-mandated ACs are present where applicable: E005 (docs-authoring) has the Rule 24 \"technically reviewed against the implemented UI\" AC; feature-flag/rollback-style ACs are present on both E003 and E004 (\"with the flag disabled, no Feature Store admin UI changes are visible\") even though this is a new capability rather than a replacement (Rule 23); no konflux chain exists, so Rule 25 is N/A. E001's ACs are report-deliverable conditions (each with an explicit \"or the gap is documented with a remediation proposal\" branch). No schedule-constraint ACs misfiled (lab turnaround / review-board cadence patterns absent). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — E004's dependencies appear only in frontmatter, and bodies refer to work streams descriptively (\"the FeatureStore CRD validation work\", \"the frontend implementation\").\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy scope is accounted for: create wizard, management list, detail/inspect, delete flow, real-time status, viewer tier, air-gapped support, feature flag, RBAC extension, prototype reuse, UXD design, and admin-guide documentation each land in a named epic. All 7 proposed strategy acceptance criteria map to E003/E004/E005 ACs. Documentation Support is required (prerequisites note admin-guide docs needed, Documentation Team listed as authors) and E005 exists to satisfy it. The conditional branch covers the bounded investigation outcome (operator/CRD gaps → BRANCH-B-E006 remediation; no gaps → epic dropped; field-set divergence → E004 rewrite gate). Strategy-level context is carried forward rather than dropped: every open question and needs-validation assumption has an explicit disposition (investigation, resolved-by-out-of-scope, or health warning), and the risk table items reappear as epic ACs/notes (UXD capacity → health warning + E002 notes; CRD stability → E001/E004 notes; viewer RBAC bypass → E003 ACs and notes; pod resource growth → E004 notes). Out-of-scope items (editing, permissions UI, multi-tenant) are correctly excluded, with the stale editing open question flagged as a health warning rather than silently resolved.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48164,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af90472888fa9bb6","agent_id":"a10e9db46b4e557b2","session_id":"f4ee95a6-a773-43fc-83d6-721cce8a6ac9","uuid":"47358552-060d-46c2-839a-c7ce61ab5860","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:23:23.134Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
